WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.234
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.677
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.977 --> 00:00:15.147
Unit thirty-three: The Future of Work. In this unit, you will talk about how work will be in the future.

4
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.047
remote work.

5
00:00:17.747 --> 00:00:21.337
remote work means working from a place outside the office, often at home.

6
00:00:21.637 --> 00:00:24.670
Remote work became common after 2020.

7
00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:27.941
Your turn. Say: remote work.

8
00:00:30.641 --> 00:00:31.630
remote work.

9
00:00:32.617 --> 00:00:33.502
freelancer.

10
00:00:34.202 --> 00:00:38.256
freelancer means a person who works for different clients, not one company.

11
00:00:38.556 --> 00:00:42.309
As a freelancer, she designs websites for clients around the world.

12
00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:45.359
Your turn. Say: freelancer.

13
00:00:48.059 --> 00:00:49.084
freelancer.

14
00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.142
gig economy.

15
00:00:51.842 --> 00:00:55.514
gig economy means work made of many short jobs, often through apps.

16
00:00:55.814 --> 00:00:58.394
Delivery riders are part of the gig economy.

17
00:00:59.094 --> 00:01:01.560
Your turn. Say: gig economy.

18
00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:05.401
gig economy.

19
00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:07.685
job security.

20
00:01:08.385 --> 00:01:11.743
job security means knowing that your job will not be taken away.

21
00:01:12.043 --> 00:01:14.971
Government jobs usually offer good job security.

22
00:01:15.671 --> 00:01:18.556
Your turn. Say: job security.

23
00:01:21.256 --> 00:01:22.442
job security.

24
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.683
digital skills.

25
00:01:25.383 --> 00:01:29.148
digital skills means the ability to use computers and the internet well.

26
00:01:29.448 --> 00:01:32.457
Digital skills are needed in almost every job today.

27
00:01:33.157 --> 00:01:35.879
Your turn. Say: digital skills.

28
00:01:38.579 --> 00:01:39.952
digital skills.

29
00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:41.765
retraining.

30
00:01:42.465 --> 00:01:45.556
retraining means learning new skills for a different job.

31
00:01:45.856 --> 00:01:48.959
Many factory workers need retraining for new jobs.

32
00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:51.928
Your turn. Say: retraining.

33
00:01:54.628 --> 00:01:55.792
retraining.

34
00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:57.982
workplace.

35
00:01:58.682 --> 00:02:00.809
workplace means the place where you work.

36
00:02:01.109 --> 00:02:03.677
A friendly workplace makes employees happier.

37
00:02:04.377 --> 00:02:06.972
Your turn. Say: workplace.

38
00:02:09.672 --> 00:02:10.754
workplace.

39
00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:13.065
coworking space.

40
00:02:13.765 --> 00:02:17.575
coworking space means a shared office where people from different companies work.

41
00:02:17.875 --> 00:02:20.235
He rents a desk in a coworking space.

42
00:02:20.935 --> 00:02:23.448
Your turn. Say: coworking space.

43
00:02:26.148 --> 00:02:27.486
coworking space.

44
00:02:28.483 --> 00:02:30.471
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:30.771 --> 00:02:33.514
What do you think work will be like in 2040?

46
00:02:34.817 --> 00:02:38.790
I think many people will be working from home or in coworking spaces.

47
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:42.176
Will robots be doing most jobs?

48
00:02:43.483 --> 00:02:48.051
Some, yes. That's why retraining and digital skills will be so important.

49
00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:52.592
This time next year, I'll be working as a freelancer!

50
00:02:53.883 --> 00:02:58.033
Great! Just remember that freelancers don't always have job security.

51
00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:01.918
Grammar focus: Future continuous.

52
00:03:02.218 --> 00:03:07.120
Use the future continuous for an action that will be in progress at a time in the future.

53
00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:08.561
Will be plus -ing.

54
00:03:08.861 --> 00:03:12.892
For example: This time next year, I will be studying in Japan.

55
00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:18.651
We often use it with time phrases like this time next week, at 8 p.m. tomorrow and in ten years.

56
00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:22.871
Now read and listen. Work in 2040.

57
00:03:23.171 --> 00:03:28.480
Experts predict that in 2040 many people will be working with AI tools every day.

58
00:03:29.783 --> 00:03:34.058
Remote work and coworking spaces will be more common than traditional offices.

59
00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:38.464
Millions of people will be earning money in the gig economy.

60
00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:43.863
Workers will need regular retraining to keep their digital skills up to date.

61
00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:49.773
The workplace of the future will be flexible, but job security may be harder to find.

62
00:03:51.083 --> 00:03:53.503
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:53.803 --> 00:03:56.442
A person who works for different clients is a blank.

64
00:03:56.742 --> 00:04:00.639
A, freelancer. B, workplace. C, coworking space.

65
00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.963
The answer is A: freelancer.

66
00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:10.577
At nine tonight, I blank my homework.

67
00:04:10.877 --> 00:04:13.997
A, will be doing. B, will do. C, am do.

68
00:04:17.983 --> 00:04:19.774
The answer is A: will be doing.

69
00:04:21.283 --> 00:04:24.850
In 2040, people blank in flying taxis.

70
00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:28.664
A, will be travelling. B, travelled. C, have travelled.

71
00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:34.557
The answer is A: will be travelling.

72
00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:38.793
Learning new skills for a different job is blank.

73
00:04:39.093 --> 00:04:42.781
A, retraining. B, job security. C, remote work.

74
00:04:46.783 --> 00:04:48.597
The answer is A: retraining.

75
00:04:50.083 --> 00:04:53.372
According to the text, what will workers need regularly?

76
00:04:53.672 --> 00:04:57.534
A, more holidays. B, retraining. C, bigger offices.

77
00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.236
The answer is B: retraining.

78
00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:08.389
Now it's your turn to speak. What will you be doing in ten years' time?

79
00:05:13.689 --> 00:05:19.172
In ten years, I'll be working as an engineer, and I'll probably be living in a city near the sea.

80
00:05:19.472 --> 00:05:20.949
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:25.903
Great work today! You learned eight new words and future continuous.

82
00:05:26.203 --> 00:05:29.633
Today's value is hard work. Work hard and never give up.

83
00:05:29.933 --> 00:05:32.272
See you in Unit thirty-four. Goodbye!

84
00:05:32.572 --> 00:05:35.375
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

